    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0450" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/757.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President Oreste and the Haitian Foreign Office jointly request that the
                    Department have the <hi rendition="#italic">Nashville</hi> go to Fort Liberty
                    with <pb facs="0451" n="335" xml:id="pg335"/> orders to Pradel, Minister of the
                    Interior and in command there, to return to Port au Prince. The Government is
                    unable to communicate with Pradel, who is cut off and who is urgently needed
                    here as the strongest man to preserve order.* * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
